Nomla
Copyright (C) 2026 The Nomla Authors (see AUTHORS)

Nomla is a Mumble voice-chat client for Android. It is a port of Mumla
(https://gitlab.com/quite/mumla, Daniel Lublin and contributors), which is a
fork of Plumble (https://github.com/acomminos/Plumble, Andrew Comminos). Its
protocol and audio library, Humla (libraries/humla, libraries/humla-protocol),
comes from Humla (https://gitlab.com/quite/humla, Daniel Lublin and
contributors), a fork of Jumble (https://github.com/acomminos/Jumble, Andrew
Comminos). Nomla has been almost completely rewritten, from Java to Kotlin;
files derived from Mumla, Humla, Plumble or Jumble keep the copyright notices
of their original authors.

